WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.728
TritonAI Harness is UC San Diego's AI workspace on your desktop.

2
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:08.420
You hand it real work, and it delivers finished results,

3
00:00:08.679 --> 00:00:10.773
using your files and campus systems.

4
00:00:11.623 --> 00:00:15.682
Here it is, live, with a made-up project: Jordan's fall workshop pilot.

5
00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:18.486
Qualtrics already reports the survey,

6
00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:20.995
but Jordan wants the team's own questions answered,

7
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.270
so I hand it the raw results.

8
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.189
Fourteen seconds later: averages for every question, the top comments,

9
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:32.175
the missing data flagged, and a takeaway for the planning team,

10
00:00:32.607 --> 00:00:33.582
saved as a file.

11
00:00:35.232 --> 00:00:39.219
Department leaders want one page, so: a presentation-ready Excel dashboard.

12
00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:44.198
It builds the workbook, and a few quick follow-ups polish the layout.

13
00:00:45.048 --> 00:00:48.652
Headline numbers up top, three charts in campus colors,

14
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.162
and a one-line insight under each.

15
00:00:52.012 --> 00:00:54.343
Jordan has ten minutes with leaders next week,

16
00:00:54.626 --> 00:00:57.109
so the meeting notes and the survey become

17
00:00:57.129 --> 00:00:59.988
a briefing deck on the official UC San Diego template.

18
00:01:00.838 --> 00:01:03.383
Nine slides with live charts, an owners table,

19
00:01:03.477 --> 00:01:07.661
a timeline to the next session, and speaker notes,

20
00:01:07.681 --> 00:01:09.464
all built from the source files.

21
00:01:10.314 --> 00:01:16.522
It plugs into the campus systems you already use: Microsoft 365,

22
00:01:16.813 --> 00:01:19.933
Google Workspace, Kuali Build, GitHub, and n8n.

23
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:26.238
Here it reads an n8n workflow, explains each step in plain language,

24
00:01:26.474 --> 00:01:28.331
and confirms the last run succeeded.

25
00:01:30.581 --> 00:01:35.136
With GitHub, it reviews a code change: what changed, which files,

26
00:01:35.466 --> 00:01:36.916
and whether the build passed.

27
00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:40.679
And it builds software.

28
00:01:41.515 --> 00:01:43.576
A Microsoft Form would cover a basic sign-up,

29
00:01:43.596 --> 00:01:46.383
but Jordan's team wants the campus look

30
00:01:46.403 --> 00:01:49.432
and every sign-up in its own n8n workflow.

31
00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:52.606
Here's that app, on the official campus design system.

32
00:01:54.256 --> 00:01:56.900
Coming soon: self-service hosting,

33
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.083
so the apps you build

34
00:01:58.103 --> 00:02:00.351
in the Harness can go live for campus.

35
00:02:01.201 --> 00:02:03.871
When a campus tool does the job, use it.

36
00:02:04.443 --> 00:02:07.337
When you need it your way, build it with the Harness.

37
00:02:08.187 --> 00:02:12.914
That's TritonAI Harness: real work, finished on your desktop,

38
00:02:13.201 --> 00:02:14.711
with campus tools built in.
